## Reference SHACL shapes for the fluent/scene-graph pattern.
##
## Push into a dataset's own `shacl` graph (conn.shapes_graph) to enable
## the gating that holonbridge.fluent.update_fluent() checks against.
##
## Corrects a bug found during scratch testing (2026-08-12): an earlier
## draft of holon:FluentPropertyRangeShape used
## `sh:targetObjectsOf holon:fluentProperty`, which validates the WRONG
## triple pattern -- it checked the object of the *link* property
## (holon:fluentProperty, added this session, connecting a Fluent instance
## to which FluentProperty type it instantiates) rather than the pattern
## the shape's own name and original intent describe: any DOMAIN predicate
## declared `a holon:FluentProperty` (e.g. `Account:hasValue`) must, in its
## own usage anywhere in the graph, point at a holon:Fluent. Those are two
## different constraints on two different properties, and the first draft
## validated the wrong one -- confirmed against a live SHACL endpoint
## (full-mode validate_turtle), not merely re-read. Fixed below by giving
## each pattern its own shape.

@prefix holon: <https://w3id.org/holon/> .
@prefix hevt:  <https://w3id.org/holon/event/> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix sh:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .

## Any predicate declared `a holon:FluentProperty` must, wherever it is
## used as a predicate, point at a holon:Fluent -- never a direct literal
## or entity value. A SPARQL target, not a static sh:targetObjectsOf on one
## fixed predicate, because the set of FluentProperty-typed predicates is
## open: any domain can declare a new one (e.g. Account:hasValue) without
## this shape needing to know its name in advance.
holon:FluentPropertyRangeShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:comment "Any predicate declared a holon:FluentProperty must, wherever used, point at a holon:Fluent -- never a direct literal or entity value."@en ;
    sh:target [
        a sh:SPARQLTarget ;
        sh:select """
            PREFIX holon: <https://w3id.org/holon/>
            SELECT ?this WHERE {
                ?predicate a holon:FluentProperty .
                ?s ?predicate ?this .
            }
        """ ;
    ] ;
    sh:class holon:Fluent .

## The correct constraint for holon:fluentProperty itself (added this
## session): its object is the FluentProperty type descriptor a Fluent
## instantiates -- e.g. Account:AccountBalanceProperty -- which must be a
## holon:FluentProperty, not a holon:Fluent. Distinct shape, distinct
## pattern; the bug above came from conflating this one with the shape
## above.
holon:FluentPropertyLinkRangeShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:comment "holon:fluentProperty links a Fluent instance to the FluentProperty type it instantiates -- its object must be a holon:FluentProperty (the type descriptor), never a holon:Fluent."@en ;
    sh:targetObjectsOf holon:fluentProperty ;
    sh:class holon:FluentProperty .

## Verified correct as originally written -- both a positive case (a clean
## supersession chain conforms) and a negative case (a deliberately
## inserted rogue StateAssertion that neither supersedes the prior current
## assertion nor is invalidated) were run against a live SHACL endpoint.
## The negative case correctly flagged both sides of the overlapping pair.
holon:StateAssertionNonOverlapShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:comment "For a given hevt:forFluent, at most one non-invalidated hevt:StateAssertion may exist without being superseded by another non-invalidated one."@en ;
    sh:targetClass hevt:StateAssertion ;
    sh:sparql [
        sh:message "This StateAssertion's fluent has more than one current (non-invalidated, non-superseded) assertion." ;
        sh:select """
            PREFIX hevt: <https://w3id.org/holon/event/>
            SELECT $this WHERE {
                $this hevt:forFluent ?fluent .
                FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this hevt:invalidatedAt ?anyInvalidation }
                FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?later hevt:supersedes $this }
                FILTER EXISTS {
                    ?other hevt:forFluent ?fluent .
                    FILTER (?other != $this)
                    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?other hevt:invalidatedAt ?anyOtherInvalidation }
                    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?laterOther hevt:supersedes ?other }
                }
            }
        """ ;
    ] .
